{"Using `\".\" << website_host` mutates the receiver string, which can behave unpredictably with shared or frozen string literals (e.g., `frozen_string_literal: true` will raise)": 0.36566901206970215, "In `website_name`, consider parsing the URI only once and reusing both the parsed object and the `host`/`path` to avoid repeated `URI(website.to_s)` calls": 0.08667588233947754, "The `website_name` logic does multiple `split('.')` operations on `website_host` and `discourse_host`; factoring these into local variables would make the branching easier to follow and less error-prone": 0.024196181446313858, "Rescuing all exceptions with `URI(website.to_s).host rescue nil` is too broad; it would be safer to rescue only `URI::InvalidURIError` or validate the URL earlier to avoid masking unexpected errors": 0.45835840702056885, "The host comparison logic in `website_name` is intricate; adding small helper methods for 'same host', 'same parent domain', etc. would make the intent clearer and reduce edge-case bugs": 0.049865610897541046}